// Pseudocode: an explicit compiler primitive for repeated member storage.
// This storage contract is not implemented yet.
@builtin("many")
macro many(): Member

// The annotated member holds a variable number of element slots, stored out
// of line. Its declared type supplies the element type; C uses only that
// type's layout, never its name. Macros such as @collection apply @many;
// user declarations do not.
//
// Primitive operations on the member, used only through its owner:
// - resize(to: n): make exactly n slots available, keeping existing ones.
// - read(at: i): the element in slot i.
// - write(at: i, value: v): store v in slot i.
//
// @many does not track count, capacity, or growth policy; the owning macro
// declares those as ordinary members. The member is not a standalone value.
//
// Open: behavior for out-of-range slots; layout computation for Element;
// the allocator behind resize.
